                <pb facs="0703" n="579" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg579"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.00/851: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harvey</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-10-14T12:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 14,
                                1923—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received October 15—9:20
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>438. My 436, October 12, 1 p.m.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d514-f1"/> The Foreign
                    Office has issued the following statement: <pb facs="0704" n="580"
                        xml:id="pg580"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“His Majesty’s Government have accepted the invitation of the French
                            Government to send representatives to the conference at Paris on October
                            22nd on the subject of the future status of Tangier.</p>
                        <p>The conference will be limited to representatives of Great Britain,
                            France and Spain. The British representatives will be Mr. Arnold
                            Robertson, His Majesty’s Agent and Consul General at Tangier and Mr.
                            Gerald Villiers, Counsellor at the Foreign Office.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harvey</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
